{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1514017-designing-the-panopticon-infrastructure-and-angels","id":1514017,"title":"Designing the Panopticon: Infrastructure and Angels","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-06T08:49:48-07:00","id":1514017,"title":"Designing the Panopticon: Infrastructure and Angels","content":"I'm revisiting a scenario I never got to run originally, and didn't want to do any thread necromancy. In my city of Buena Vista, the God-Machine recently built a piece of Infrastructure called the Panopticon for creating and sustaining a Rank 3 angel named Jeremiel. Its Mission is to monitor social media and electronic communications to identify local supernatural creatures, specifically some changelings who've sabotaged Infrastructure and Occult Matrices. What I have written right now:<br /> <br /> Virtue: Vigilant<br /> Vice: Cautious<br /> Influence: Data 3<br /> Ban: Jeremiel must stop whatever it's doing to perform online research if given a formally or technically phrased request.<br /> Bane: Ink made through antiquated means.<br /> <br /> I always feel like I'm missing something when I try to come up with Bans, Banes and similar weaknesses for my antagonists and monsters. The Ban I have here seems appropriate for an Analyst angel that's expected to report findings to its command Infrastructure, and a way for player characters to buy time in a confrontation, and the Bane is a reference to using &quot;antiquated&quot; methods like letter writing to avoid electronic monitoring. In Jeremiel's case, I'm having some difficulty figuring out how players might discover these weaknesses. If they can't find out, they might as well not exist. Jeremiel has only been operating for a few years, so I struggle to imagine how players might do proper research. (Though it occurs to me that players might compel Jeremiel to research its own bane for irony.)<br /> <br /> I'm open to ideas for angels and other God-Machine things in the city:<ul><li>Hunter angels to send if mortal agents aren't enough to neutralize the saboteurs.</li> <li>Defenses to protect the Panopticon. It's attached to three skyscrapers with tech company offices, so there's mortal security forces, at least.</li> <li>Surveillance agents for supplementing the electronic searches.</li> <li>Social agents to bribe or threaten supernatural players into cooperating with the Machine.</li> <li>Any ideas for other God-Machine projects in the city. The Panopticon was made to identify and eliminate saboteurs, so they need some things worth sabotaging.</li> </ul>I'm still getting a feel for handling the God-Machine, so I could use advice on how to calibrate the mechanics if/when I get a group. I'm hoping for a Chronicle climax where experienced changeling players and their allies infiltrate the Panopticon and bring it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}